<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lucius Munatius Plancus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 87–c. 15 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lucius Munatius Plancus was a Roman general and politician. A legate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>, he founded the colonies of Lugdunum (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lyon">Lyon</a>) and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augusta-raurica">Augusta Raurica</a> around 44–43 BCE, and later changed sides between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a> and Octavian. In 27 BCE he proposed in the Senate that Octavian take the name Augustus. His mausoleum stands at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaeta">Gaeta</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lucius-munatius-plancus.jpg" alt="Lucius Munatius Plancus" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 2.0 fr · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bust_of_Plancus_IMG_9753.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
